# Human-facing docs (warm-precise)

Write clear, confident, human prose. Short sentences. No jokes, marketing taglines, or hype.

## Product facts (never violate)

- `mcpx` is a **CLI client**, not an MCP server/gateway. Never document editing Cursor/IDE `mcp.json` as an mcpx feature.
- Tool commands always require explicit Server (`-s` / `--server`).
- Never invent features; stay aligned with `INCEPTION.md`, `FEATURES.md`, and shipped CLI (`docs/cli.md`).

## Domain terms

Capitalize per `CONTEXT.md`: Server, Purpose, Tool, Config, Output, Agent Guide, Adapter, Transport.

`CONTEXT.md` itself stays definitional — do not warm-rewrite the glossary when polishing landing docs.

## Landing / README shape

- Open with problem → product hook when introducing mcpx.
- Hybrid thinness: keep a real quickstart; deep-link the full CLI to `docs/cli.md`.
- Prefer scannable sections; avoid encyclopedia walls on landing pages.
- One mental-model mermaid diagram when it clarifies the agent loop (list Servers → list Tools → call Tool). No decorative diagrams.
- Honest badges only (no aspirational npm/CI). Stack details belong in a footer, not the hero.
- Use a See also for glossary (`CONTEXT.md`) and backlog (`FEATURES.md`) — don’t bury the product hook under link dumps.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
> The ultimate MCP gateway for every IDE 🚀
![npm](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/mcpx)  <!-- not published yet -->

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
Shell CLI that reaches configured MCP Servers by running commands.
See also: [CONTEXT.md](./CONTEXT.md), [FEATURES.md](./FEATURES.md). Full CLI: [docs/cli.md](./docs/cli.md).
```

## ADRs (`docs/adr/`)

Stay factual and decision-focused; skip warm marketing voice.
